Traceability: Graph

Purpose:
  Defines traceability requirements and chain validation.

TraceabilityChain:
  PROMPT
    ↓
  REQUIREMENT
    ↓
  DECISION
    ↓
  TASK
    ↓
  WORKFLOW
    ↓
  SKILL
    ↓
  CODE
    ↓
  BDD
    ↓
  TEST
    ↓
  SECURITY
    ↓
  INFRA
    ↓
  DEPLOYMENT
    ↓
  RUNTIME
    ↓
  INCIDENT
    ↓
  DOCUMENT

ReverseTraceability:
  INCIDENT
    ↓
  CODE
    ↓
  TASK
    ↓
  DECISION

TraceabilityScore:
  Overall: <percentage>
  Code → Task: <percentage>
  Task → Requirement: <percentage>
  Task → Test: <percentage>
  Task → Security: <percentage>
  Decision → Code: <percentage>
  Incident → Code: <percentage>
  Docs → Code: <percentage>

BrokenChain:
  TRACE-BROKEN:
    Chain incomplete between nodes
  WORKFLOW-BROKEN:
    Workflow stage not completed

TraceabilityRules:
  [TR1]  Every task MUST trace to a requirement.
  [TR2]  Every code change MUST trace to a task.
  [TR3]  Every test MUST trace to a task.
  [TR4]  Every incident MUST trace to code.
  [TR5]  Broken chains MUST be detected and reported.
  [TR6]  Traceability score MUST be calculated regularly.

